Z||000000||Homicidal||08-06-2000||12:36 AM||||I used Pherder's car as an example!<P> <IMG SRC="http://albums.photopoint.com/j/View?u=208525&a=1537447&p=20813971&Sequence=0"> <P>Where can I get these so clear and how much?  Mine are a bit cracked and OH so faded!||||reg||1
Z||000001||BN Boomer||08-06-2000||01:20 AM||||Phew, for a minute there I thought you were trying to disgrace your Fiero with those crappy clear lenses that the rice boys are so fond of.||||reg||1
Z||000002||My7Fieros||08-06-2000||01:35 AM||||PHEW!!! Me too! Dont scare me like that Homicidal!!! <BR>I took mine off and used a platic buffing compound. It came in a tube, kinda chalky, blue or brown in color. I applied it with a buffing wheel on a drill. Looks clear again! Hardware stores carry it.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif">||||reg||1
Z||000003||HugGRRRFiero||08-06-2000||01:51 AM||||   First, I took apart my tailights cleaned them with good old soap and water.  Then I used some Meguires plastic polish on a soft towel and buffed my colored lenses and clear covers.  Sorry, I've used the same bottle for so long I can't remember where I got the polish, but I think you can get it some at a paint supply store.  It seemed to help brighten mine.<P>Brent<P>------------------<BR>   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/huggrrr.gif"> <BR> <A HREF="mailto:HugGRRRFiero@hotmail.com">HugGRRRFiero@hotmail.com</A> ||||reg||3
Z||000004||Monkeyman||08-06-2000||01:59 AM||||If you can't find the plastic polish anywhere else and you're close to a large truckstop, try there.  Also ask at your local body shop.||||reg||1
Z||000005||Monkeyman||08-06-2000||02:04 AM||||Of course, you can always copy me (OK.  The Grape Ape came this way.) and lightly spray your tail lights with paint.  Then it doesn't matter if they're perfectly clear or not.  This pic is from when WT III and I picked up my car.  Pardon the dirt.  It had been sitting for 6 months.<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/GrapeApe-rear.JPG"> <BR>||||reg||1
Z||000006||Homicidal||08-06-2000||02:32 AM||||I did have a moment of insanity on the clear lights.  But I came to my senses when I realized how TRENDY that is.  I AM going to pic up some brighter bulbs though.  Mine are very old and faded.  Does anyone know what kind I should buy?  Model # and such?<P>Ok, so it's a plastic buffing compound?  And it will lighten the plastic?<P>Well, first I am going to goto the boneyard and pic up one in better shape.  I saw a few. I can also get some almost brand new looking gels (the red and white plastic things).  But will the compound take out the "smoked" look to it?  BTW, how long is the process?||||reg||1
Z||000007||My7Fieros||08-06-2000||02:55 AM||||It only took me about 20 or 30 minutes to do the lenses. Youll need a helper..someone to hold them while you buff them (if you use a buffing wheel on a drill like I did).<BR>They really came out great! Really "shined" them up..you know, took that hazy look out and made them look new again.<BR>That Mcquires stuff will work great to Im sure..I just like to use a buffing wheel on a drill, I just think its more thorough.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif">||||reg||1
Z||000008||BAM-BAM||08-06-2000||10:35 PM|||| Homicidal, If you don't have any luck, I have a set in my garage that are already polished up and ready to go. E-Mail me if and when you think you might be in need. The lens's are perfect no cracks or scratches. Just a couple of the tabs are broken, but you'll never see them anyway. LMK<P> Late, BAM OUT!   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"><P>------------------<BR>Don B. <BR>85GT<p>[This message has been edited by BAM-BAM (edited 08-06-2000).]||||reg||12
